s highly collaborative, and a wide range of research is conducted. Current research areas include medicinal chemistry, biochemistry, bioinorganic chemistry, cellular and molecular biology, computational chemistry, biophysics, microbiology, neuroscience, pharmacometrics, pharmacokinetics, drug formulation, drug transport and delivery, industrial pharmaceutical research, and translational and regulatory sciences. Research is interdisciplinary and students have access to state-of-the-art facilities that include centers in nanobiotechnology, mass spectrometry, computer aided drug design and translational medicine.\nMS Program Home\nPhD Program Home\nApply\nDetails, Dates & Deadlines\nProgram Details\nClass Format\nIn-Person, Full Time\nProgram Location\nUMB Campus (PhD and MS)\nUniversities at Shady Grove (MS)\nCost/Credit Hour\nMaster's:\nStudent Financial Services\nDoctoral/PhD:\nThe PhD in PSC program is fully funded for accepted students\nPlease note that this doesn\u2019t apply to the MS in PSC program\nCore Requirements\nLearn more about the application requirements\nPhD requirements\nMS requirements\nDates & Deadlines\nFall deadline: March 1 (MS program)\nFall deadline: December 1 (PhD program)\nPharmaceutical Sciences\nAdmissions\nErika Pixley, MBA\nAssociate Director of Admissions\nOffice of Graduate Programs\nsopgradadmissions@rx.umaryland.edu\n410-706-8056\nPhD Program\nAmanda Oglesby, PhD\nDirector, PhD in Pharmaceutical Sciences\naoglesby@rx.umaryland.edu\nMS Program\nSteven Fletcher, PhD\nDirector, MS in Pharmaceutical Sciences\nsfletcher@rx.umaryland.edu\nNext Steps\nYour path to success starts here\nRequest Information\nRegister for an Info Session\nApply\nPrograms\nDirections\nSupport\nContact Us\nUMB Careers\nMobile UMB\nUMB Shuttle\nThe ELM\nUniversity of Maryland School of Graduate Studies\n620 W. Lexington St.\nBaltimore, MD 21201\n(410) 706-3100\nTwitter\nYouTube\nInstagram\nFacebook\nUniversity of Maryland School of Graduate Studies. All Rights Re